<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10064" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cōnexĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conn-</span></b> ),
		ōnis, f.
		conecto, t. t. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A binding together, close union</i>, etc.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scutorum, armorum (in a testudo),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 18, 12, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. A. 9, 517</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Esp.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>An organic union;</i> cf. Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 35, 13</span></i> Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animae et corporis nostri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Psa. 118, 7, §
				7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			philos. lang. (almost confined to Quint.), <i>a
				conclusion, a logical sequence</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 5,
				14, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">17</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">19</span></i>; 22
			sq.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> In gram., <i>a syllable</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Charis. p. 1</span></i> P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
